# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Note:** CPU time is the post-processing time. The three mirror circuits were submitted together in one run, so the recorded QPU and CPU times are for all three circuits together. Each Clifford circuit run contained nine PUBs with different circuit depths, so the recorded times are for all nine PUBs together. Each Ising circuit run contained 10 PUBs with different numbers of Trotter steps, so the recorded times are for all 10 PUBs together.\n"
msgstr "**Tandaan:** Ang CPU time ay ang oras ng post-processing. Magkakasamang isinumite sa isang run ang tatlong mirror circuit, kaya ang naitalang QPU at CPU time ay para sa lahat ng tatlong circuit nang magkakasama. Ang bawat run ng Clifford circuit ay may siyam na PUB na may iba't ibang circuit depth, kaya ang naitalang oras ay para sa lahat ng siyam na PUB nang magkakasama. Ang bawat run ng Ising circuit ay may 10 PUB na may iba't ibang bilang ng Trotter step, kaya ang naitalang oras ay para sa lahat ng 10 PUB nang magkakasama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the mirror circuits, the benchmarks use the RealAmplitudes, TwoLocal, and EfficientSU2 ansätze with 30, 35, and 40 qubits, respectively. The observables consist of a single Pauli-$Z$ operator on a randomly selected qubit, with an ideal expectation value of 1.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga mirror circuit, gumagamit ang mga benchmark ng mga ansatz na RealAmplitudes, TwoLocal, at EfficientSU2 na may 30, 35, at 40 qubit, ayon sa pagkakasunod. Binubuo ang mga observable ng iisang Pauli-$Z$ operator sa isang random na napiling qubit, na may ideal na expectation value na 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the Clifford circuits, the benchmarks use 50- and 100-qubit circuits with observables initialized as one or more randomly positioned Pauli-$Z$ operators. Operator evolution increases the Pauli weight of these observables, which provides more complex observables for benchmarking. The observables are constructed to have an ideal expectation value of 1, which is independently verified with stabilizer simulation.\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga Clifford circuit, gumagamit ang mga benchmark ng mga circuit na may 50 at 100 qubit na may mga observable na sinimulan bilang isa o higit pang random na nakaposisyong Pauli-$Z$ operator. Pinapataas ng operator evolution ang Pauli weight ng mga observable na ito, na nagbibigay ng mas masalimuot na mga observable para sa benchmarking. Binuo ang mga observable para magkaroon ng ideal na expectation value na 1, na hiwalay na beneripika gamit ang stabilizer simulation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the Trotterized 2D tilted-field Ising (TFI) Hamiltonian simulations, the benchmarks use three parameter regimes: small angle $(\\theta_X,\\theta_Z,\\theta_{ZZ})=(0.1,0.1,0.1)$, near-Clifford $(0.1,0.05,1.5708)$, and chaotic $(0.53,0.1,1.0)$. The observable is the average magnetization,\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga simulation ng Trotterized 2D tilted-field Ising (TFI) Hamiltonian, gumagamit ang mga benchmark ng tatlong parameter regime: small angle $(\\theta_X,\\theta_Z,\\theta_{ZZ})=(0.1,0.1,0.1)$, near-Clifford $(0.1,0.05,1.5708)$, at chaotic $(0.53,0.1,1.0)$. Ang observable ay ang average magnetization,\n"

