# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Like the Estimator primitive, the LTM AI-QEM function accepts primitive unified blocs (PUBs) as input. A PUB is a tuple of the form `(circuit, observables, parameter_values, precision)`, where `parameter_values` is required for parametric circuits and `precision` is optional.\n"
msgstr "Tulad ng Estimator primitive, tumatanggap ang LTM AI-QEM function ng primitive unified blocs (PUBs) bilang input. Ang PUB ay isang tuple na may anyong `(circuit, observables, parameter_values, precision)`, kung saan kailangan ang `parameter_values` para sa mga parametric na circuit at opsyonal ang `precision`.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit {#circuit}"
msgstr "Circuit {#circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $n$-qubit Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger (GHZ) state is given by:\n"
"$$\n"
"|GHZ\\rangle_{n}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert{0}\\rangle^{\\otimes{n}} + \\vert{1}\\rangle^{\\otimes{n}}}{\\sqrt2}\n"
"= \\frac{\\overbrace{\\vert{00}\\dots{0}\\rangle}^{\\text{$n$ qubits}} + \\overbrace{\\vert{11}\\dots{1}\\rangle}^{\\text{$n$ qubits}}}{\\sqrt2}.\n"
"$$\n"
"To construct the $n$-qubit GHZ state, initialize all qubits in the $|0\\rangle$ state and apply a Hadamard gate to the first qubit to create an equal superposition. Then apply a sequence of CNOT gates across the entire register, with qubit $i$ as the control and qubit $i+1$ as the target. This staircase of entangling gates propagates the initial superposition to all qubits, which results in the entangled GHZ state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $n$-qubit na Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger (GHZ) state ay ibinibigay ng:\n"
"$$\n"
"|GHZ\\rangle_{n}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert{0}\\rangle^{\\otimes{n}} + \\vert{1}\\rangle^{\\otimes{n}}}{\\sqrt2}\n"
"= \\frac{\\overbrace{\\vert{00}\\dots{0}\\rangle}^{\\text{$n$ qubits}} + \\overbrace{\\vert{11}\\dots{1}\\rangle}^{\\text{$n$ qubits}}}{\\sqrt2}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Para buuin ang $n$-qubit na GHZ state, i-initialize ang lahat ng qubit sa $|0\\rangle$ state at maglapat ng Hadamard gate sa unang qubit para makagawa ng pantay na superposition. Pagkatapos, maglapat ng sunod-sunod na CNOT gate sa buong register, na ang qubit $i$ ang control at ang qubit $i+1$ ang target. Ang hagdang ito ng mga entangling gate ay nagpapalaganap ng paunang superposition sa lahat ng qubit, na nagreresulta sa entangled na GHZ state.\n"

# doq: translated after #1094 review 2026-11-21
#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observables {#observables}"
msgstr "Mga Observable {#observables}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring the two-body tensor product $Z_i \\otimes Z_j$ on a GHZ state evaluates the parity correlation between any two qubits in the register. Because the GHZ state is a superposition of the all-zeros and all-ones states, any two qubits are perfectly correlated. The eigenvalue is $(+1 \\times +1) = 1$ for the $\\vert00\\dots0\\rangle$ branch and $(-1 \\times -1) = 1$ for the $\\vert11\\dots1\\rangle$ branch. Because both branches return +1, the theoretical expectation value is 1. Construct the observable with the `SparsePauliOp` class.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagsukat ng two-body tensor product na $Z_i \\otimes Z_j$ sa isang GHZ state ay sumusuri sa parity correlation ng alinmang dalawang qubit sa register. Dahil ang GHZ state ay superposition ng all-zeros at all-ones na mga state, perpektong magkorelasyon ang alinmang dalawang qubit. Ang eigenvalue ay $(+1 \\times +1) = 1$ para sa branch na $\\vert00\\dots0\\rangle$ at $(-1 \\times -1) = 1$ para sa branch na $\\vert11\\dots1\\rangle$. Dahil +1 ang ibinabalik ng parehong branch, 1 ang theoretical na expectation value. Buuin ang observable gamit ang `SparsePauliOp` class.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the circuit is not parametric, construct the PUB as `(circuit, observable)`.\n"
msgstr "Dahil hindi parametric ang circuit, buuin ang PUB bilang `(circuit, observable)`.\n"

