# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 2: Mirror circuit {#example-2-mirror-circuit}"
msgstr "Halimbawa 2: Mirror circuit {#example-2-mirror-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses a mirror circuit to calculate expectation values of observables passed in PUBs of different shapes. It demonstrates the LTM AI-QEM function and its compatibility with different PUB shapes, and compares the mitigated results with the unmitigated results.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang halimbawang ito ng mirror circuit para kalkulahin ang mga expectation value ng mga observable na ipinasa sa mga PUB na may iba't ibang hugis. Ipinapakita nito ang LTM AI-QEM function at ang compatibility nito sa iba't ibang hugis ng PUB, at ikinukumpara ang mga mitigated na resulta sa mga unmitigated na resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A mirror circuit applies a randomly generated circuit and then its inverse. In an ideal, noiseless execution, the two halves cancel and return the qubits to their initial state. This makes the circuit useful for studying how hardware and runtime noise affect an otherwise predictable result.\n"
msgstr "Ang mirror circuit ay naglalapat ng random na nabuong circuit at pagkatapos ay ng inverse nito. Sa ideal at walang noise na pagpapatakbo, nagkakansela ang dalawang kalahati at ibinabalik ang mga qubit sa paunang state nila. Dahil dito, kapaki-pakinabang ang circuit para pag-aralan kung paano nakakaapekto ang noise ng hardware at runtime sa isang resultang kung hindi man ay mahuhulaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this example, you construct multiple PUBs. Each PUB pairs the same mirror circuit with observables, made up of Pauli operators, that are given in different shapes.\n"
msgstr "Sa halimbawang ito, bubuo ka ng maraming PUB. Pinagpapares ng bawat PUB ang iisang mirror circuit sa mga observable na binubuo ng mga Pauli operator, na may iba't ibang hugis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The LTM AI-QEM function evaluates these observables and returns both the expectation values from the noisy execution and the values after mitigation. This example has two goals: to verify that the function accepts the supported PUB formats, and to compare the mitigated expectation values with the noisy values to see how effectively the error mitigation workflow restores the expected behavior of the mirror circuit.\n"
msgstr "Sinusuri ng LTM AI-QEM function ang mga observable na ito at ibinabalik ang parehong mga expectation value mula sa noisy na pagpapatakbo at ang mga value pagkatapos ng mitigation. May dalawang layunin ang halimbawang ito: beripikahin na tinatanggap ng function ang mga sinusuportahang format ng PUB, at ikumpara ang mga mitigated na expectation value sa mga noisy na value para makita kung gaano kaepektibo ang error mitigation workflow sa pagbabalik ng inaasahang gawi ng mirror circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct the PUBs {#construct-the-pubs}"
msgstr "Buuin ang mga PUB {#construct-the-pubs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each PUB is a tuple of a circuit and a list of observables. The function computes the expectation values of the observables with respect to the circuit. In this example, the circuit is the same for all of the observable configurations. You pass the list of PUBs, `pubs`, to `ltm_function` to run.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat PUB ay isang tuple ng isang circuit at isang listahan ng mga observable. Kinakalkula ng function ang mga expectation value ng mga observable kaugnay ng circuit. Sa halimbawang ito, pareho ang circuit para sa lahat ng configuration ng observable. Ipapasa mo ang listahan ng mga PUB, `pubs`, sa `ltm_function` para patakbuhin.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit {#circuit-1}"
msgstr "Circuit {#circuit-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, create a mirror circuit with five qubits. To do this, create a random circuit with the Qiskit `random_circuit` function. Specify the number of qubits (`n_qubits=5`), the circuit depth (`depth=5`), and a seed for reproducibility (`seed=42`). Then add a `barrier` at the end of the random circuit, and use `unitary_overlap` to create the mirror circuit. Because `unitary_overlap(U1, U2)` creates the circuit that corresponds to $U_{2}^{\\dagger}U_{1}$, passing the same circuit as both arguments creates the mirror circuit. The `barrier` prevents the circuit from becoming the identity during transpilation. The code output shows the depth of the mirror circuit, which is expected to be about 10 for `depth=5`, plus the barrier layers.\n"
msgstr "Una, gumawa ng mirror circuit na may limang qubit. Para dito, gumawa ng random na circuit gamit ang Qiskit `random_circuit` function. Tukuyin ang bilang ng mga qubit (`n_qubits=5`), ang depth ng circuit (`depth=5`), at isang seed para sa reproducibility (`seed=42`). Pagkatapos, magdagdag ng `barrier` sa dulo ng random na circuit, at gamitin ang `unitary_overlap` para buuin ang mirror circuit. Dahil ang `unitary_overlap(U1, U2)` ay gumagawa ng circuit na tumutugma sa $U_{2}^{\\dagger}U_{1}$, ang pagpasa ng parehong circuit bilang dalawang argument ay lumilikha ng mirror circuit. Pinipigilan ng `barrier` na maging identity ang circuit habang nagta-transpile. Ipinapakita ng output ng code ang depth ng mirror circuit, na inaasahang mga 10 para sa `depth=5`, dagdag ang mga layer ng barrier.\n"

# doq: translated after #1094 review 2026-11-21
#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observables {#observables-1}"
msgstr "Mga Observable {#observables-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, create the lists of observables whose expectation values you want to compute, in different formats. First, define the variables `ALL_X_PAULI = XXXXX`, `ALL_Y_PAULI = YYYYY`, and `ALL_Z_PAULI = ZZZZZ`, which represent the corresponding Pauli observables on all five qubits.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, gumawa ng mga listahan ng mga observable na gusto mong kalkulahin ang mga expectation value, sa iba't ibang format. Una, tukuyin ang mga variable na `ALL_X_PAULI = XXXXX`, `ALL_Y_PAULI = YYYYY`, at `ALL_Z_PAULI = ZZZZZ`, na kumakatawan sa mga katumbas na Pauli observable sa lahat ng limang qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then define `obs_1` as a list of three observables. The first is a linear combination of two Pauli operators, $0.3\\,ZZZZZ + 0.5\\,XXXXX$, defined as a `SparsePauliOp`. The second is `SparsePauliOp([ALL_Z_PAULI])`, also a `SparsePauliOp`. The third is the Pauli string `ALL_X_PAULI`. The PUB with `obs_1` has an observable array of shape `(3,)`.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos, tukuyin ang `obs_1` bilang listahan ng tatlong observable. Ang una ay linear combination ng dalawang Pauli operator, $0.3\\,ZZZZZ + 0.5\\,XXXXX$, na tinukoy bilang `SparsePauliOp`. Ang pangalawa ay `SparsePauliOp([ALL_Z_PAULI])`, na isa ring `SparsePauliOp`. Ang pangatlo ay ang Pauli string na `ALL_X_PAULI`. Ang PUB na may `obs_1` ay may observable array na may hugis na `(3,)`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, define `obs_2` in a matrix layout, that is, as a list of lists, where each inner list contains observables of type `SparsePauliOp` or Pauli strings. The first row contains `ALL_X_PAULI` and $0.3\\,ZZZZZ + 0.5\\,YYYYY$. The second row contains $0.3\\,XXXXX + 0.5\\,ZZZZZ$ and $2.0\\,ZZZZZ$. The PUB with `obs_2` has an observable array of shape `(2, 2)`.\n"
msgstr "Panghuli, tukuyin ang `obs_2` sa matrix layout, ibig sabihin, bilang listahan ng mga listahan, kung saan ang bawat panloob na listahan ay naglalaman ng mga observable na may uri na `SparsePauliOp` o mga Pauli string. Ang unang hilera ay naglalaman ng `ALL_X_PAULI` at $0.3\\,ZZZZZ + 0.5\\,YYYYY$. Ang pangalawang hilera ay naglalaman ng $0.3\\,XXXXX + 0.5\\,ZZZZZ$ at $2.0\\,ZZZZZ$. Ang PUB na may `obs_2` ay may observable array na may hugis na `(2, 2)`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collect the two PUBs as `pubs = [(mirror_circuit, obs_1), (mirror_circuit, obs_2)]`.\n"
msgstr "Kolektahin ang dalawang PUB bilang `pubs = [(mirror_circuit, obs_1), (mirror_circuit, obs_2)]`.\n"

