# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 4: Brickwork Clifford circuit {#example-4-brickwork-clifford-circuit}"
msgstr "Halimbawa 4: Brickwork Clifford circuit {#example-4-brickwork-clifford-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example simulates Clifford circuits. This family of circuits is useful because you can design the simulation to have a known expectation value. Specifically, you can design the circuit and the observable so that the expectation value is always 1, as follows:\n"
msgstr "Sinisimulate ng halimbawang ito ang mga Clifford circuit. Kapaki-pakinabang ang pamilyang ito ng mga circuit dahil maaari mong idisenyo ang simulation para magkaroon ng kilalang expectation value. Partikular, maaari mong idisenyo ang circuit at ang observable para laging 1 ang expectation value, tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The starting point (the stabilizer):** Start with the vacuum state $|0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$. Applying the Pauli $Z$ or the identity operator to $|0\\rangle$ leaves it unchanged: $Z|0\\rangle = |0\\rangle$ and $I |0\\rangle = |0\\rangle$. Therefore, any Pauli string $P$ that is a tensor product of only $Z$ and $I$ leaves the all-zero state $|0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$ unchanged: $P |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n} = |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$.\n"
msgstr "**Ang panimulang punto (ang stabilizer):** Magsimula sa vacuum state na $|0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$. Ang paglalapat ng Pauli $Z$ o ng identity operator sa $|0\\rangle$ ay nag-iiwan dito na hindi nagbabago: $Z|0\\rangle = |0\\rangle$ at $I |0\\rangle = |0\\rangle$. Kaya, anumang Pauli string na $P$ na tensor product ng $Z$ at $I$ lamang ay nag-iiwan sa all-zero state na $|0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$ na hindi nagbabago: $P |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n} = |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The Clifford evolution:** Applying the unitary $U_L$ to the state gives $|\\psi\\rangle = U_L |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$. To find an observable whose expectation value for this new state is 1, apply the same unitary transformation to the operator: $O_L = U_L P U_L^{\\dagger}$. This is the Heisenberg picture of quantum mechanics.\n"
msgstr "**Ang Clifford evolution:** Ang paglalapat ng unitary na $U_L$ sa state ay nagbibigay ng $|\\psi\\rangle = U_L |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$. Para makahanap ng observable na 1 ang expectation value para sa bagong state na ito, ilapat ang parehong unitary transformation sa operator: $O_L = U_L P U_L^{\\dagger}$. Ito ang Heisenberg picture ng quantum mechanics.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Why the observable stays a single Pauli string:** If $U_L$ contained non-Clifford gates (such as T gates or arbitrary rotations), $U_L P U_L^\\dagger$ would expand into a sum of many different Pauli strings. You would have to measure many different observables and add them to get 1. However, because the circuit uses only Clifford gates, the Gottesman-Knill theorem guarantees that $U_L P U_L^\\dagger$ maps to exactly one Pauli string (for example, $X Y -Z X$).\n"
msgstr "**Bakit nananatiling iisang Pauli string ang observable:** Kung ang $U_L$ ay may mga non-Clifford na gate (tulad ng mga T gate o arbitrary na rotation), ang $U_L P U_L^\\dagger$ ay lalawak at magiging kabuuan ng maraming magkakaibang Pauli string. Kakailanganin mong sukatin ang maraming magkakaibang observable at pagsamahin ang mga ito para makakuha ng 1. Gayunpaman, dahil mga Clifford gate lang ang ginagamit ng circuit, ginagarantiya ng Gottesman-Knill theorem na ang $U_L P U_L^\\dagger$ ay nagma-map sa eksaktong isang Pauli string (halimbawa, $X Y -Z X$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The mathematical guarantee:** Because of this construction, computing the expectation value is a simple algebraic substitution:\n"
msgstr "**Ang mathematical na garantiya:** Dahil sa konstruksyong ito, ang pagkalkula ng expectation value ay isang simpleng algebraic na pagpapalit:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle O_L \\rangle = \\langle \\psi | O_L | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle O_L \\rangle = \\langle \\psi | O_L | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Substitute $|\\psi \\rangle$ and $O_L$:\n"
"$$\n"
"(\\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} U_L^{\\dagger})\n"
"(U_L P U_L^{\\dagger})\n"
"(U_L | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipalit ang $|\\psi \\rangle$ at $O_L$:\n"
"$$\n"
"(\\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} U_L^{\\dagger})\n"
"(U_L P U_L^{\\dagger})\n"
"(U_L | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n})\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The adjacent $U_L^\\dagger U_L$ terms cancel (they equal the identity $I$):\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} P | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagkakansela ang magkatabing terminong $U_L^\\dagger U_L$ (katumbas ng mga ito ang identity na $I$):\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} P | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $P$ is a tensor product of only $Z$ and $I$, $P| 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n} = | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n}$, and therefore:\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n} = 1\n"
"$$\n"
"First, design quantum circuits that contain only Clifford gates: the single-qubit gates $H$, $S$, $X$, $Y$, and $Z$, and the two-qubit gate $CZ$. The `create_brickwork_clifford` function takes the number of qubits (`num_qubits`) and `depth` as arguments, and returns a Clifford quantum circuit with the given number of qubits and depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil ang $P$ ay tensor product ng $Z$ at $I$ lamang, $P| 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n} = | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n}$, at samakatuwid:\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n} = 1\n"
"$$\n"
"Una, magdisenyo ng mga quantum circuit na may mga Clifford gate lamang: ang mga single-qubit na gate na $H$, $S$, $X$, $Y$, at $Z$, at ang two-qubit na gate na $CZ$. Ang function na `create_brickwork_clifford` ay tumatanggap ng bilang ng mga qubit (`num_qubits`) at `depth` bilang mga argument, at nagbabalik ng Clifford quantum circuit na may ibinigay na bilang ng mga qubit at depth.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuits in this example have 50 qubits (`num_qubits=50`) and varying depths: 30, 35, 40, 45, 50, 55, 60, 65, and 70. For the observables, start from a Pauli string $P$ with Pauli weight 2, that is, two Pauli $Z$ operators at random positions. Then use the `evolve` method to evolve $P$ into $U_{L_i} P U_{L_i}^{\\dagger}$ for the circuit $U_{L_i}$ of each depth. Save the circuits and the corresponding observables in the lists `circuits_list` and `observables_list`, respectively.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga circuit sa halimbawang ito ay may 50 qubit (`num_qubits=50`) at iba't ibang depth: 30, 35, 40, 45, 50, 55, 60, 65, at 70. Para sa mga observable, magsimula sa isang Pauli string na $P$ na may Pauli weight na 2, ibig sabihin, dalawang Pauli $Z$ operator sa mga random na posisyon. Pagkatapos, gamitin ang `evolve` method para i-evolve ang $P$ tungo sa $U_{L_i} P U_{L_i}^{\\dagger}$ para sa circuit na $U_{L_i}$ ng bawat depth. I-save ang mga circuit at ang mga katumbas na observable sa mga listahang `circuits_list` at `observables_list`, ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To get the ideal values, run a stabilizer simulation. Create a stabilizer state from each quantum circuit with the Qiskit `StabilizerState` class, which takes a `QuantumCircuit` as input and outputs the corresponding stabilizer state. Then use the `expectation_value` method to calculate the ideal expectation value, which by design is 1 for each circuit and observable pair.\n"
msgstr "Para makuha ang mga ideal na value, magpatakbo ng stabilizer simulation. Gumawa ng stabilizer state mula sa bawat quantum circuit gamit ang Qiskit `StabilizerState` class, na tumatanggap ng `QuantumCircuit` bilang input at naglalabas ng katumbas na stabilizer state. Pagkatapos, gamitin ang `expectation_value` method para kalkulahin ang ideal na expectation value, na sa disenyo ay 1 para sa bawat pares ng circuit at observable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, create a list of PUBs named `clifford_pubs` and pass it to `ltm_function` to compute the expectation values on hardware and mitigate them with AI-QEM.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, gumawa ng listahan ng mga PUB na pinangalanang `clifford_pubs` at ipasa ito sa `ltm_function` para kalkulahin ang mga expectation value sa hardware at i-mitigate ang mga ito gamit ang AI-QEM.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extract and visualize the results {#extract-and-visualize-the-results-2}"
msgstr "I-extract at i-visualize ang mga resulta {#extract-and-visualize-the-results-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the job finishes, collect the expectation values and standard deviations from each PUB result. For every circuit depth, the results include the noisy (unmitigated) values, `noisy_evs` and `noisy_stds`, and the values after mitigation by AI-QEM, `mitigated_evs` and `mitigated_stds`.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos matapos ang job, kolektahin ang mga expectation value at standard deviation mula sa bawat resulta ng PUB. Para sa bawat circuit depth, kasama sa mga resulta ang mga noisy (unmitigated) na value, `noisy_evs` at `noisy_stds`, at ang mga value pagkatapos ng mitigation gamit ang AI-QEM, `mitigated_evs` at `mitigated_stds`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then use the `plot_clifford_results` function to plot the expectation value against the circuit depth. The plot contains the following:\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos, gamitin ang `plot_clifford_results` function para i-plot ang expectation value laban sa circuit depth. Naglalaman ang plot ng mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Unmitigated:** The raw expectation values returned by the hardware, shown with error bars of size $\\pm\\sigma$.\n"
msgstr "**Unmitigated:** Ang mga raw na expectation value na ibinalik ng hardware, na ipinapakita kasama ng mga error bar na may laking $\\pm\\sigma$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Mitigated (AI-QEM):** The expectation values after error mitigation, also shown with error bars.\n"
msgstr "**Mitigated (AI-QEM):** Ang mga expectation value pagkatapos ng error mitigation, na ipinapakita rin kasama ng mga error bar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ideal (stabilizer simulation):** The noiseless expectation value, $\\langle O \\rangle_{\\text{ideal}} = 1$, for all depths.\n"
msgstr "**Ideal (stabilizer simulation):** Ang walang-noise na expectation value, $\\langle O \\rangle_{\\text{ideal}} = 1$, para sa lahat ng depth.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Threshold:** A gray band that covers $-0.1 \\le \\langle O \\rangle \\le 0.1$. Values inside this band have no useful signal to mitigate, so they are left unmitigated.\n"
msgstr "**Threshold:** Isang gray na band na sumasaklaw sa $-0.1 \\le \\langle O \\rangle \\le 0.1$. Ang mga value sa loob ng band na ito ay walang kapaki-pakinabang na signal na ima-mitigate, kaya iniiwan ang mga ito na unmitigated.\n"

